=== AUD-UA-3 (coupon double-subtract) ===
Cart: Almond Milk 1L x5 @ 4.80 AED = subtotal 24.00 AED (Daily Fresh Market, zone 1).
Applied coupon NEARS2924PCT (percent, discount=10.00, min_purchase=20.00) via the Checkout
screen's "Enter Promo Code" + Apply.

uiautomator dump (bounds-ordered) after Apply:
  y=2325 Subtotal            24.00 AED
  y=2421 Discount             0.00 AED
  y=2517 Coupon Discount     -2.40 AED   <- exactly 10% of 24.00, ONE subtraction
  y=2596 Total Amount        22.68 AED

DB row for the resulting order (placed at 11:21:27):
  id=91213 order_amount=22.68 coupon_discount_amount=2.40 coupon_code=NEARS2924PCT
  payment_method=cash_on_delivery order_status=pending

2.40 = 10% x 24.00 subtracted exactly ONCE (a double-subtract would show 4.80 / a ~19.20-20.28
total). PASS — no regression on AUD-UA-3.

=== AUD-UA-4 (place-order double-submit) ===
Cart: Cheddar Block x1 @ 14.22 AED (Daily Fresh Market, zone 1), no coupon.
Baseline: `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM orders WHERE user_id=3` = 5 (before this sub-test).

Rapid double-tap on "Place Order" (two `adb shell input tap 672 1858` issued back-to-back,
no sleep between):

App log (only ONE "place-order button clicked" for the whole double-tap):
  09-08 11:25:19.359  I flutter : [INFO] msg="checkout: place-order button clicked"
  09-08 11:25:19.360  I flutter : [INFO] msg="multipart POST endpoint=/api/v1/customer/order/place"
  09-08 11:25:21.505  I flutter : [NET] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/order/place http_status=200
  (no second "place-order button clicked" / no second POST anywhere in the log — the
  `_isLoading` guard at checkout_controller.dart:2401-2403 swallowed the second tap before it
  ever logged, matching the NEARS-720 fix's intent)

DB after: `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM orders WHERE user_id=3` = 6 (+1, exactly one new row, id=91214,
order_amount=14.93, created_at 2026-09-08 11:25:25).

PASS — no regression on AUD-UA-4 (exactly one order created per double-tap, exactly one
POST /api/v1/customer/order/place, exactly one "place-order button clicked" log line).
